            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 11-year-old girl with a history of trichophagia presented with abdominal pain and progressive vomiting. The MRI scan showed a gastric mass and multiple masses in the small intestine. A large trichobezoar was removed from the stomach by laparotomy.</AbstractText>
